{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Gate/CI status before push.\n\nFull CI pytest invocation (-m 'not integration and not external' -n 3 --dist worksteal --timeout=300) on the pre-rebase tree: 12600 passed, 60 skipped, 1 FAILED. The failure was MINE and is now fixed: tests/interfaces/store/test_canonical_event_bytes.py asserted cross-producer canonical event bytes and got its SNAPSHOT coverage implicitly, by closing a throwaway ticket and letting compact-on-close fold it (its own comment said 'closing auto-compacts'). With the trigger gone the SNAPSHOT writer stopped running, so the test's own type-coverage guard fired — working exactly as designed.\n\nFixed by making the fold EXPLICIT (rebar.compact(snap)) rather than incidental, with REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD=1 and REBAR_COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS=0 so a small freshly-written ticket actually folds (the default threshold and horizon would both skip it, and a silently skipped fold would drop SNAPSHOT from the coverage set again). Note threshold must be >= 1 — the config coercion rejects 0. The test now states in a comment why the compact is explicit, so the next person does not re-couple it to a close.\n\nThat was the only test in the tree coupled to compact-on-close as a side effect.\n\nRebased onto origin/main, which had moved to ae6f2ac57a 'Pin the gate ticket store to the live store' — change 1700, the verifier store-pinning fix. It composes cleanly: 1700 changes which ticket store the gate READS, this change removes a post-close store WRITE; no shared surface, no conflict. Post-rebase re-verified: complexity baseline active=59 new=0 increased=0 stale=0, mypy clean (518 files), all five generators re-run with zero diff, wall-clock-assert / raw-git-write / comment-hygiene gates clean.\n\nNon-test diff is 115 lines (61 added, 54 deleted), under the 150-line bugfix-size-attestation threshold, and a signed plan attestation is on file regardless.\n\nLocal rebar review-code is a no-op in this checkout (verify.enable_code_review is off), so the Gerrit LLM-Review bot is the first code review this change sees. Re-running the full suite on the rebased tree now; pushing once it is green."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786597705276491001,"uuid":"6b73c445-66b4-4cae-845e-36c08cbf6f24"}